            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0736" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">551.5F1/147: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-07T17:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>88. Legation’s 99, July 28, 5 p.m. Your proposal to have Germany present a
                    resolution on a silver conference to the League of Nations meets with our
                    approval. You should confidentially push it. Our Ambassador in Germany<anchor
                        n="54" xml:id="d481-f1"/> is being informed of these proceedings but advised
                    not to initiate anything. This Government attaches great importance to the
                    silver problem. Consequently, you should be very active but discreet in the
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="54" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
